.TH PHPVPN-TRAY 1 "2026-09-26" "phpvpn 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
phpvpn-tray \- tray application of the phpvpn service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B phpvpn-tray
.RB [ \-\-show\-window ]
.RB [ \-\-installation\-complete ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B phpvpn-tray
shows the connection state of the local
.BR phpvpn-service (8)
as an icon in the desktop notification area (StatusNotifierItem through
AppIndicator) and offers the same actions as the Windows tray: Connect or
Disconnect, the Configuration Wizard, Communication contracts, Edit Config,
Show Server Info, Statistics and Exit. It talks to the service over the control
socket
.I /run/phpvpn/control-v1.sock
and needs no root.
.PP
The tray does not own the VPN connection. Exit, logging out and the end of the
desktop session close only the tray; the connection stays as it is. At startup
the tray reads the state and never connects on its own.
.PP
One instance runs per desktop session (application ID
.BR org.phpvpn.Tray ).
A second start passes its arguments to the running instance and exits.
.PP
When the desktop offers no StatusNotifierItem host, for example GNOME on Fedora
Workstation without the AppIndicator extension, the tray opens a control window
with the state and the same actions instead, and shows a notification once that
explains how to enable the extension. The icon appears by itself once a host is
available.
.SH OPTIONS
Without an option the tray only shows its icon; the autostart entry starts it
this way.
.TP
.B \-\-show\-window
Show the control window of the running instance. The application launcher
.I phpvpn-tray.desktop
uses this option.
.TP
.B \-\-installation\-complete
Show the installation notice through the desktop notification service.
.PP
Other arguments are ignored.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The tray ended normally, or a second start passed its arguments to the running
instance.
.TP
.B 1
No graphical display could be opened (neither
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
nor
.B DISPLAY
works), or the tray could not initialise.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/autostart/phpvpn-tray.desktop
Starts the tray at every graphical login of every user. A user disables it for
the own account with an entry
.I ~/.config/autostart/phpvpn-tray.desktop
that contains
.BR Hidden=true .
.TP
.I /usr/share/applications/phpvpn-tray.desktop
Application launcher, runs
.BR "phpvpn-tray \-\-show\-window" .
.TP
.I /run/phpvpn/control-v1.sock
Control socket of the service. The tray only talks to a peer running as root.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR phpvpn (1),
.BR phpvpn-service (8),
.BR gnome-extensions (1)
